# Traditional Database Access

Without JPA, you'd write JDBC code like this:

```java
Connection conn = DriverManager.getConnection(url, user, pass);
PreparedStatement stmt = conn.prepareStatement("SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?");
stmt.setLong(1, id);
ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery();
while (rs.next()) {
    User user = new User();
    user.setId(rs.getLong("id"));
    user.setName(rs.getString("name"));
    ...
}
```

This is **verbose**, error‑prone, and mixes SQL with Java code.

**JPA** (Java Persistence API) is a standard that lets you work with databases using plain Java objects (POJOs).
